# Interpreters of ours whose plugins are native code: an arm64 package's
# dependency on one of these is met by Debian's arm64 build only
# (usr/lib/gex/all-foreign), so its XS module or extension gets an
# interpreter that can load it, in place of ours. Extended regular
# expressions, one a line; `<<` after one: only a dependency with an upper
# version bound (a compiled python extension's).
perlapi-[0-9.]+
python3 <<
python3\.[0-9]+ <<
